//? Title: Clockwork RNN: Explicit Masking, State Paths and Source Controls
//? Subtitle: Native recurrent tensor components and an editable source training loop
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The original clockwork rnn experiment is retained with source fixtures, parameter initialization, full state histories and gradient controls. Reusable model math lives in datamunge; the complete C++ program below owns training, optimizer writes, checkpoints and diagnostic queries.
)
\toc

> Source experiment and explicit tensor workflow

The source uses a small synthetic single-marker sequence-memory task. These are mechanism experiments with the original short budgets, rather than real-data benchmark claims. Optional TensorFlow replay is skipped when its recordings are absent. The program preserves every recorded state, input/initial-state derivative, padding/causality control and source checkpoint.

> Read the state, mask and update separately

Four three-unit modules tick at periods 1,2,4,8. The recurrent matrix is masked so a slow module can feed a faster one, and each state update is also gated by valid sequence length. The source records module-specific input derivatives and exact held-state checks.

The original pools contain512 fitting,128 validation and 128 test sequences, with twelve padded timesteps, two input channels, balanced alternating classes and a marker before the final valid token. Each ordinary fit uses Adam(.01),32-row batches and three epochs:48 updates. All synthetic draws and source IDs are recorded by the canonical generator.

The report introduces 206 learned values in the actual source graph. Valid lengths are structural inputs, while hidden/cell tensors and weights retain live derivative paths. Inference receives inputs, lengths and explicit initial states; targets belong to the objective only.

